## 10. Exact next obligation

For each of the four linear-defect branches in (PE.11), prove at least one source-level consequence strong enough to close the full-core branch:

\[
\boxed{
\text{linear PE defect}
\Longrightarrow
\text{strict same-cardinality sub-}D\text{ competitor or exact unit triangle.}
}
\]

The most immediate branch-specific targets are:

- charge linear `m_B` to actual loaded-interior incidence/equilibrium and then to a diameter-decreasing exchange;
- convert linear `Q-f` into a quantitative high-degree-face/corridor obstruction;
- couple linear `b-p` directly to the audited aggregate-detour identity;
- show linear `tau_D` forces additional interface/chamber currency beyond the existing near-geodesic regressions.

No claim is made here that any one of these four implications is already proved.

